UID:CGngD1ZH9f
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nIn Kiwi Chow’s drama-thriller\
 , an elite academy drives students to pills\, rebellion\, and a suicide ul
 timatum—exposing an authority-soaked system through stunning visuals and
  standout young performances. Producer Peiyi Lin scheduled to attend.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/festival/deadline\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ShortsFest Opening Night
DTSTART:20260509T020000Z
DTEND:20260509T035000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T020000Z
UID:iA9gVEHeFX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nIt is our great pleasure to open 
 our ShortsFest Spotlight with this collection of superb films from around 
 the world: whether narrative or documentary\, live action or animation—t
 hese films prove short is truly sweet.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sh
 ortsfest-opening-night-x41555\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broken English
DTSTART:20260509T043000Z
DTEND:20260509T062500Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T043000Z
UID:wiRlqPWm24
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nSinger-songwriter and actress Mar
 ianne Faithfull is too big for a simple documentary. Instead\, a theatrica
 l “Department of Not Forgetting” interweaves intimate interviews\, arc
 hival clips\, and newly recorded performances to conjure a holistic unders
 tanding of a career spanning more than half a century.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/festival/broken-english\n\nEstimated start: 21:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
